lede: >-
  Deep learning algorithms learn multi-level representations of data, with each level explaining the data at a higher
  level of abstraction. They have been remarkably effective at uncovering structure in data and have driven progress in
  image classification, speech recognition, and natural language processing.
about: >-
  <p>Taught through lectures and projects, the course covers the underlying theory, the range of problems deep learning
  has been applied to, and learning from very large datasets. We study fully connected, convolutional, recurrent, and
  graph neural networks, with a focus on how to train and optimize them and use them for effective inference. Students
  work throughout in PyTorch.</p>
